<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.thefixinhixon.SplosionManRecomp</id>
  <name>SplosionManRecomp</name>
  <summary>Native PC port of 'Splosion Man (Xbox 360)</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.thefixinhixon">
    <name>thefixinhixon</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.thefixinhixon.SplosionManRecomp.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
    <binary>SplosionManRecomp</binary>
  </provides>

  <description>
    <p>
      SplosionManRecomp is a native Linux port of 'Splosion Man, Twisted Pixel's
      2009 Xbox Live Arcade platformer, made by static recompilation with the
      ReXGlue SDK.
    </p>
    <p>
      No game data is included. You need your own legally obtained copy of the
      game's XBLA package: the launcher imports it, or you can point it at an
      extracted game folder.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Unlocked frame rate and low input latency</li>
      <li>In-game options menu (F1, or both sticks): frame cap, VSync, AMD FSR and CAS upscaling, resolution, audio and controls</li>
      <li>Controller with vibration, or keyboard</li>
      <li>A launcher that explains every setting in plain language</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      An unofficial fan project, not affiliated with Twisted Pixel Games or Microsoft.
    </p>
  </description>

